        "original_id": "e70e21f3-ed43-51b2-b1ca-64d7d8718f5a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Olive Kitteridge, Saturday Night Live, Meatballs, Caddyshack, Stripes, Tootsie, Ghostbusters, Scrooged, Ghostbusters II, What About Bob?\n- People: Frances McDormand, Richard Jenkins, Zoe Kazan, Bill Murray, Jane Anderson\n- Places: Maine\n- Awards: Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Bill Murray first gained exposure on Saturday Night Live, and his performances there earned him his first Emmy Award.\n- Bill Murray later starred in the comedy films Meatballs (1979), Caddyshack (1980), Stripes (1981), Tootsie (1982), Ghostbusters (1984), Scrooged (1988), Ghostbusters II (1989), and What About Bob?.\n- In 2014, Jane Anderson won an Emmy Award for writing the screenplay for the miniseries Olive Kitteridge.\n- Olive Kitteridge is an HBO miniseries set in Maine.\n- In Olive Kitteridge, Frances McDormand plays the title character, Richard Jenkins plays Olive's husband Henry Kitteridge, Zoe Kazan plays Denise Thibodeau, and Bill Murray plays Jack Kennison.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
